      "body": "\n\n## Overview\nReduce GIL contention in EngineCore's output thread by avoiding redundant PyTorch operations when exporting contiguous CPU tensors for serialization. This is a follow-up of sorts to #61640, has a similar motivation, and addresses a similar problem, this time in the EngineCore output thread.\n\n\n## Claims\n- Improve embedding throughput on short inputs by **7.5% at concurrency 128** and **2.6% at concurrency 64** on the GH200 workload below, with no request errors.\n- Reduce contiguous CPU FP32 export latency from **4.61 µs to 1.10 µs** and GIL releases from **7 to 1** per call.\n- Reuse existing `EMBED_DTYPES` metadata for BF16/FP8 views and preserve the original conversion path for other inputs.\n\n\n\n## Validation\n\nExisting serialization, buffer-lifetime, and prompt-embedding hashing tests:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/utils_/test_serial_utils.py \\\n  tests/v1/test_serial_utils.py \\\n  tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py \\\n  -k 'serial or prompt_embeds' -q\n```\n\n\n**End-to-end performance**: `nvidia/Nemotron-3-Embed-1B-BF16` (`--quantization fp8_per_tensor`,\n  `--api-server-count 16`), `/v1/embeddings`, ViDoRe v3 finance-en queries (~30 tokens each),\n  closed-loop client on the other NUMA node, 1× GH200, `orjson` in use. Mean of 3 × 30 s runs.\n\n  | Concurrency | Metric | main | this PR | Change |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 64 | Throughput (req/s) | 4,482 | 4,600 | **+2.6%** |\n  | 64 | p50 latency (ms) | 14.26 | 13.87 | −2.7% |\n  | 64 | p99 latency (ms) | 14.97 | 15.04 | +0.5% |\n  | 128 | Throughput (req/s) | 6,601 | 7,093 | **+7.5%** |\n  | 128 | p50 latency (ms) | 19.37 | 18.04 | −6.9% |\n  | 128 | p99 latency (ms) | 20.72 | 18.85 | −9.0% |\n\n  **Per call** (`tensor_data()` on a contiguous 2048-element CPU tensor):\n\n  | dtype | main | this PR | Speedup | GIL releases (main → PR) |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | float32 | 4.61 µs | 1.10 µs | 4.2× | 7 → 1 |\n  | float16 | 4.44 µs | 1.10 µs | 4.1× | — |\n  | bfloat16 | 4.78 µs | 3.83 µs | 1.25× | 7 → 3 |\n  | float8_e4m3fn | 4.53 µs | 3.84 µs | 1.18× | — |\n## Details\nThe original chain releases and reacquires the GIL repeatedly even when the tensor is already contiguous and on CPU. This overhead adds contention when the output thread serializes many small tensors during concurrent serving.\n\nThe fast path exports a NumPy-backed byte memoryview directly. A precomputed `torch.dtype` lookup derives only non-identity views from `EMBED_DTYPES`: BF16 is viewed as FP16, and the two supported FP8 formats as uint8. This preserves the raw bytes without maintaining another dtype list or adding unnecessary `.view()` calls for NumPy-supported formats. If NumPy export fails, serialization falls back to the original chain.\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
