    "body": "\n\n## Overview\nReduce GIL contention in EngineCore's output thread by avoiding redundant PyTorch operations when exporting contiguous CPU tensors for serialization. This is a follow-up of sorts to #61640, has a similar motivation, and addresses a similar problem, this time in the EngineCore output thread.\n\n\n## Claims\n- Improve embedding throughput on short inputs by **7.5% at concurrency 128** and **2.6% at concurrency 64** on the GH200 workload below, with no request errors.\n- Reduce contiguous CPU FP32 export latency from **4.61 µs to 1.10 µs** and GIL releases from **7 to 1** per call.\n- Reuse existing `EMBED_DTYPES` metadata for BF16/FP8 views and preserve the original conversion path for other inputs.\n\n\n\n## Validation\n\nExisting serialization, buffer-lifetime, and prompt-embedding hashing tests:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/utils_/test_serial_utils.py \\\n  tests/v1/test_serial_utils.py \\\n  tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py \\\n  -k 'serial or prompt_embeds' -q\n```\n\n\n**End-to-end performance**: `nvidia/Nemotron-3-Embed-1B-BF16` (`--quantization fp8_per_tensor`,\n  `--api-server-count 16`), `/v1/embeddings`, ViDoRe v3 finance-en queries (~30 tokens each),\n  closed-loop client on the other NUMA node, 1× GH200, `orjson` in use. Mean of 3 × 30 s runs.\n\n  | Concurrency | Metric | main | this PR | Change |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 64 | Throughput (req/s) | 4,482 | 4,600 | **+2.6%** |\n  | 64 | p50 latency (ms) | 14.26 | 13.87 | −2.7% |\n  | 64 | p99 latency (ms) | 14.97 | 15.04 | +0.5% |\n  | 128 | Throughput (req/s) | 6,601 | 7,093 | **+7.5%** |\n  | 128 | p50 latency (ms) | 19.37 | 18.04 | −6.9% |\n  | 128 | p99 latency (ms) | 20.72 | 18.85 | −9.0% |\n\n  **Per call** (`tensor_data()` on a contiguous 2048-element CPU tensor):\n\n  | dtype | main | this PR | Speedup | GIL releases (main → PR) |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | float32 | 4.61 µs | 1.10 µs | 4.2× | 7 → 1 |\n  | float16 | 4.44 µs | 1.10 µs |